==History==
2016
*The Elixir Collector [[Cards|card]] was added with Clash Royale's game launch on 4/1/2016.
*On 2/2/2016, the [[Version History#February 2016 Update (2/2/2016)|February 2016 Update]], increased the Elixir Collector's production time interval to 9.8 seconds (from 9.95 seconds). This was because of a bug where it would produce 6 [[Elixir]] instead of 7.
*On 29/2/2016, the [[Version History#March%202016%20Update%20(29/2/2016)|March 2016 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Elixir Collector from Royal Arena to Builder's Workshop.
*On 3/5/2016, the [[Version History#May 2016 Update (3/5/2016)|May 2016 Update]], increased the {{Rarity|Rare}} card Level cap to 11 (from 10) and decreased the Elixir Collector's hitpoints by 20%.
*On 18/5/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (18/5/2016)|Balance Update]], decreased the Elixir Collector's hitpoints by 9%.
*On 4/7/2016, the [[Version History#Tournaments Update (4/7/2016)|Tournaments Update]], made the Elixir Collector's production rate affected by spell effects ([[Freeze]], [[Zap]], and [[Rage]]), plus the [[Ice Wizard]]'s slowing.
*On 20/10/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (20/10/2016)|Balance Update]], increased the Elixir Collector's cost to 6 Elixir (from 5 Elixir) and increased its lifetime by 10 seconds. This increased lifetime allows it to produce up to 8 Elixir.
*On 30/11/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (30/11/2016)|Balance Update]], decreased the Elixir Collector's production time interval to 8.5 seconds (from 9.8 seconds) and decreased its lifetime to 70 seconds (from 80 seconds).
2017
*On 12/12/2017, the [[Version History#Electrifying Update (12/12/2017)|Electrifying Update]], decreased the Elixir Collector‘s hitpoints by 13%.
2018
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Elixir Collector from Builder's Workshop to Frozen Peak.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Rare}} cards start at Level 3 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 11).
*On 5/12/2018, the [[Version History#December%202018%20Update%20(5/12/2018)|December 2018 Update]], changed the Elixir Collector such that, if used in a [[Battle Decks|deck]], will never appear as one of the cards in the player's opening hand. Its description was also changed. Previously, its description was "''You gotta spend Elixir to make Elixir!''".
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Elixir Collector from Frozen Peak to Rascal's Hideout.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022
*On 4/4/2022, the [[Version History#April%202022%20Update%20(4/4/2022)|April 2022 Update]], decreased its lifetime to 65 seconds (from 70 seconds), increased its production time interval to 9 seconds (from 8.5 seconds), and made the Elixir Collector produce 1 additional Elixir upon death.
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Elixir Collector from Rascal's Hideout to Miner's Mine.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2024
*On 14/5/2024, the [[Version History#Balance Changes (14/5/2024)|Balance Update]], increased the production time interval to 12 seconds (from 9 seconds), but increased its lifetime to 86 seconds (from 65 seconds).
*On 1/9/2025, the September 2025 Update, added a card render to the Elixir Collector's card info screen.
2025
*On 03/11/2025 the [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/11/2025)|Balance Update]], increased the production time interval to 13 seconds (from 12 seconds), but increased its lifetime to 93 seconds (from 86 seconds).

